Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a5e: use the reference board's 936 MHz DRAM clock

The user's bootable Armbian image includes its actual U-Boot defconfig
and full .config. They explicitly select DRAM_CLK=936; all other DRAM
drive, ODT and TPR settings match the pinned mainline A5E defconfig.
Without this entry mainline selects 1200 MHz, an unvalidated change for
this board. Match the bootable reference instead of relying on that default.

Reference: Armbian build 0648ff3c4125d673c18b5f032dc7c28545c542b5,
linux-u-boot-current-radxa-cubie-a5e/u-boot-config-target-1 from the
user-provided 26.11.0-trunk.52 image. Only boot-critical SD/DRAM fixes
are imported; unrelated SPI/NVMe/PCIe enablement is not required here.

diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ CONFIG_ARM=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e"
 CONFIG_SPL=y
+CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=936
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_ODT=0x07070707
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_DRI=0x0d0d0d0d
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_CA_DRI=0x0e0e
